  "statementTechnical": "Chi (total coherence) is a bounded, non-negative, continuous scalar functional on [0,1]^9 with the following properties: (1) multiplicative product structure — not additive, (2) veto property — any single zero factor collapses the product to zero (Lean-verified), (3) C_W wrapper — coherence operator wraps the product, is not a tenth factor, currently treated as identity pending ruling, (4) dimensionless — each register enters as a fraction of its own full capacity, (5) Level 1 is a snapshot (measurement instrument), Level 2 postulates first-order open gradient dynamics over that landscape, (6) the product form is a chosen model (structurally motivated, not uniquely forced), (7) Shannon base layer carries units (bits/s) at Level 0 only — Level 1 ratios are dimensionless, (8) gradient ascent — nabla-chi points toward higher coherence under Euclidean metric on [0,1]^9 (declared), (9) the equation is a measurement instrument — it does not sanctify, and chi is not the salvation variable.",
  "statementPlain": "Chi measures how aligned a system is with what is actually true. It multiplies nine necessary channels — if any one is zero, the whole thing collapses. It is a thermometer, not a thermostat: it records where you stand, it does not move you.",
